      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the labeled maximum daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin in adults. Extended-release is labeled for up to 2,000 mg/day. Doses that high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't change the labeled limit.\n\nHere are some options that stay within the label:\n- **1700 mg per day total:** for example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Maximum IR dose:** 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day).\n- **Typo check:** if you meant 850 mg or 1000 mg per dose, tell me which. 1000 mg twice daily is 2,000 mg/day.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it."
      }
