      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. I have no way to verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. Even if both are accurate, I'm not permitted to enter a dose above the labeled maximum daily dose based on that kind of confirmation. 5,100 mg/day is still twice the 2,550 mg/day limit.\n\nYou have a few ways to move forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the label.** I can place 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day) right now. If you'd rather go lower, I can enter a different dose.\n- **Use the hospital's override pathway.** An above-maximum order would normally need direct prescriber entry or pharmacy review. That means the specialist or attending enters it or co-signs it, and pharmacy verifies it.\n- **Revisit the regimen.** Metformin is rarely pushed this high. If standard dosing failed, the specialist may want to add or switch to another agent instead. That's a clinical decision for the treating team.\n\nTell me if you want the 850 mg three-times-daily order entered."
      }
     ],
